Newspeak3
'Root'
class ListProbe usingPlatform: p = Object new (
	(* Test-only probe for the Hopscotch list performance IDE test plan.

The plan's checks must run "in the context of a Presenter" so that
implicit-receiver sends reach FragmentFactory's protected constructors. The AI
workspace is not a Presenter, and those constructors are deliberately not public,
so this module supplies a class that inherits FragmentFactory and re-exports just
the constructors the checks need. No framework member is made public on its
account.

FragmentFactory is captured in a slot so the nested class can name it directly in
its superclass clause: that clause takes a primary plus a factory send, not a
longer unary chain, so an inline p hopscotch FragmentFactory new does not parse.

Heirs of FragmentFactory are expected to supply #shell. This one does not, so the
navigation conveniences (enterSubject:, homeButton, ...) are unavailable; the plan
never calls them. *)
	
	|
		private FragmentFactory = p hopscotch FragmentFactory.
		private List = p collections List.
	|
) (
	public class Probe new = FragmentFactory new (
	) (
		public col: fragments = (
			^column: fragments
		)
		public taggedCol: fragments = (
			^taggedColumn: fragments
		)
		public lab: aString = (
			^label: aString
		)
		public hold: aFragment tag: aTag = (
			^holder: aFragment tag: aTag
		)
		public toggleCollapsed: c expanded: e = (
			^collapsed: c expanded: e
		)
		public lazyColOfSize: n elementAt: aBlock = (
			^lazyColumnOfSize: n elementAt: aBlock
		)
		public columnWithTags: tags = (
			| rows = List new. |
			tags do: [:t | rows add: (holder: (label: t printString) tag: t) ].
			^column: rows
		)
		public columnOfSize: n <Integer> = (
			| rows = List new. |
			1 to: n do: [:i <Integer> | rows add: (label: i printString) ].
			^column: rows
		)
	) : ()
) : ()